                <pb facs="0508" n="496" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg496"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.51 Frozen Credits 35/95a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-25T21:00:00-04:00">October 25, 1943—9
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1647. The President has stated with respect to the Argentine blocking proposal
                    (Department’s 1644, October 24, 8 p.m.) that he desires the proposal tabled for
                    the time being but reviewed every week or two.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
